  "//amendments": "Re-admitted on 1.21. The Fabric ban was Moonlight-chain-vs-Hephaestus: Moonlight shifted load ordering so Tinkers modifiers resolved before the dynamic modifier registry was ready. There is no Tinkers on 1.21, so that interaction cannot occur. It appears in 6/34 working reference packs. Watch item: if the join test disconnects, this is the first thing to pull.",
  "//isolation-sweep": "Ran tools/isolate.js --all-rejected on 2026-08-07 across the full reject history (current + archived 1.20.1 configs). Result: 11 have no NeoForge 1.21.1 build at all, 1 fails on a missing dependency that is not on Modrinth (create-ultimine -> ftbultimine), 1 passes and is already shipped (moonlight, via Amendments/Supplementaries). Nothing revivable remains — the reject list is accurate and does not need re-litigating.",
  "//extra-gauges": "Note: this is `extra-gauges`, NOT `create-extra-gauges` which was rejected earlier as absent from Modrinth. Different project, and this one has 10 NeoForge 1.21.1 builds.",
  "//levelling": "Tinkers' Levelling Addon 1.5.0 in overrides/mods/ — a private 1.21.1/NeoForge port of Pyre540's MIT mod (upstream stops at 1.20.1 Forge). Port work: ModDevGradle build, Forge->NeoForge package moves, SimpleChannel -> CustomPacketPayload networking rewrite, ToolAction -> ItemAbility, LevelingValue.compute(), EquipmentSlot.Type.HUMANOID_ARMOR, and a local replacement for the removed ItemStack.ATTRIBUTE_MODIFIER_FORMAT. Datagen provider excluded (build-only; JSON already committed).",
  "//external": "Mods with no Modrinth release for 1.21.1/NeoForge. Hosted as GitHub release assets (a whitelisted .mrpack download domain) so they reach players over a CDN as ordinary files[] entries instead of being embedded in overrides/. Assets are immutable: the manifest pins sha1+sha512, so a new jar build needs a NEW release tag, never a replaced asset.",
